# Read by ripgrep (Claude Code's Grep and Glob), not by git. These are data, not code: a search
# for a column name otherwise spends its whole result budget on archive JSON (3,707 of 3,866 hits
# for `runs_scored`) before reaching one line of source. To search them on purpose, pass the file
# itself as the path; a named file is never ignored.
archive/
scripts/fixtures/
package-lock.json
